import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'..')
from con_helpers import *
save(5,3,"The Technology of Attention","When your mind last wandered and you noticed it had wandered, what noticed? Spend one minute this week simply meeting that watcher.",[
mc("U","How does Conversation 5.3 describe the four stages of training attention?",
 ["Four separate techniques, each learned in turn and then left behind.","One movement at four depths, as a seedling and a flowering plant are one life.","Four tests of ability, which only a few people ever pass in a lifetime.","Four names for the same effort, which stays the same at every depth."],1,
 "The stages are turning down the volume on the senses, holding the mind on one thing, flow, and full absorption. They are not four techniques but one movement deepening, like a seedling and a flowering plant: one life at two stages.",
 "The four stages are one movement at four depths","Part 1"),
mc("A","A man holds a repeated word for four breaths, the mind slips, he brings it back, and he does this all week and feels he is failing. Which view fits Conversation 5.3?",
 ["The slips show he is not yet ready, so he should pause until his mind is calmer.","The slips are the interruptions, and the aim should be to hold the word without any.","The slipping and the bringing back are the practice, and each return builds the muscle.","The slips show his chosen word is wrong, and a different word would hold better."],2,
 "At the holding stage, dhāraṇā, the mind is meant to slip. The bringing back is the repetition that trains attention, so every time he notices and returns he strengthens exactly what he is building. He is doing the practice correctly, not failing at it.",
 "Wandering and catching is the rep: the return trains attention","Part 1"),
mc("U","In the picture of two almost matched musical notes, what does the wobble between them stand for?",
 ["The restless flicker of a mind whose note is close to its object’s note, but not yet matched.","The pleasant ripple of attention at its deepest, when mind and object are one.","The noise of the outside world, which keeps on breaking in upon the two notes.","The effort of holding the object, which grows heavier the longer the practice goes on."],0,
 "Attention is one note and its object the other. Close but not matched, they wobble, which is the slipping and the sense of me here, object there. As the notes come into tune the wobble slows and then vanishes, leaving one fuller tone. That is absorption.",
 "The wobble is the wandering of a mind not yet tuned to its object","Part 1"),
mc("A","A woman fears that deep absorption means she will vanish or lose herself. Which reply fits Conversation 5.3?",
 ["The fear is sound, and absorption should be approached only with a teacher beside her.","The flicker stills, so the steady awareness that was always there becomes plain: she is revealed.","She will lose only the thoughts, and the self she knows will remain exactly as it was.","The fear shows she is not ready, and she should stay with simpler practices for now."],1,
 "Think of a film and its screen. The thoughts and feelings are the flickering images, and the awareness that holds them never flickers. Absorption does not create that awareness; it quietens the flicker that hid it. She is not lost, she is revealed.",
 "Absorption stills the flicker and reveals the screen; no one vanishes","Part 2"),
judge("“Deep absorption creates a still awareness that was not there before, and it is built up by meditating for long enough.”",F,
 "The screen was there the whole time, overlooked behind the rush of images. Absorption does not create the witness; it quietens the flicker that was distracting you from it. When your mind wandered and you noticed, the part that noticed had not wandered. That is the screen.",
 "Absorption does not create the witness; it reveals what was always there","Part 2"),
mc("A","A teacher has settled her class and wants to train focus. Which instruction fits Conversation 5.3?",
 ["Ask them to hold one thing for sixty seconds, and say that wandering is failure to be avoided.","Ask them to hold one thing for sixty seconds, and say that noticing and returning is the training.","Ask them to sit in silence for as long as they can, and to stop if the mind wanders.","Ask them to think of something calming, and to hold it until the lesson begins."],1,
 "Calm and focus are different achievements. Telling students plainly that the mind will wander, and that the coming back is the training, lifts a quiet shame they did not know they carried. The wandering is the doorway, not the failure.",
 "Tell them that the coming back is the training","Part 1"),
mc("A","A patient reports distress, low mood, a restless body and ragged breathing, and says that meditation is not working. What does Conversation 5.3 suggest?",
 ["Treat the four signs one by one, since the signs are the trouble to be removed.","Offer the same calming practice to every such patient, with more time each day.","Tell her that the practice is not suited to her and look to some other approach.","Read these as signs of an obstacle, name it as heavy or driven, and match the practice."],3,
 "Patañjali’s four signs tell you an obstacle is active. You do not chase the signs; you treat the underlying obstacle, heavy (dullness, sloth, illness) or driven (doubt, sense-pull, distorted seeing, restlessness), and the signs fade with it.",
 "Four signs mean an obstacle: name it, match the practice, treat that","Part 3"),
judge("“The same practice that quietens the noise lets the obstacles fall away and, in one movement, makes the deeper awareness perceptible, so there is no trade-off.”",T,
 "Lower the noise floor and the static-driven troubles fade, while the quiet thing underneath, which the static was drowning out, becomes audible. One change, two faces: the medicine for the symptom and the medicine for the soul are the same medicine.",
 "One practice, two faces: easing the noise and opening the deeper door","Part 3"),
mc("A","A young man says the real enemy is his own inner commentary, which narrates, plans and worries without stopping. Which step fits Conversation 5.3?",
 ["Argue with the voice until it gives in, since a firm reply is the surest way to quiet it.","Stop feeding it: do not reply, do not rehearse its scripts, and let it thin on its own.","Drown it out by keeping the outer world busy, so that the voice is crowded off.","Listen to it closely and write down all of it, so that it has no more left to say."],1,
 "Mauna, inner silence, is the same turning down of the volume, applied within. Fighting the voice is only more inner talk, noise fought with noise. Starving it of attention is silence, and the commentary thins out the way a flame steadies when taken out of the wind.",
 "Starve the inner voice of attention instead of fighting it","Part 3"),
judge("“Deep absorption is the highest reach of the trained mind, so once it has been reached nothing more remains to be recognised.”",P,
 "The first half is right: absorption is the stillest the mind can become. But it is still a state, with the faint hum of one tone. It is the stillest the film can be, not yet the full recognition of the screen in which even absorption appears and passes. The meditation clears the view; it is not the destination.",
 "Absorption is the highest reach of the mind, yet not the end of the road","Part 3")])
